      "text": "To determine the number of the first day which ends with the colony having more than 100 bacteria, we start by understanding the growth pattern of the bacteria colony. The colony doubles every day, and it starts with 3 bacteria.\n\n1. **Day 0 (initial):**\n   - Number of bacteria: \\(3\\)\n\n2. **Day 1:**\n   - The number of bacteria doubles from \\(3\\) to \\(3 \\times 2 = 6\\).\n\n3. **Day 2:**\n   - The number of bacteria doubles from \\(6\\) to \\(6 \\times 2 = 12\\).\n\n4. **Day 3:**\n   - The number of bacteria doubles from \\(12\\) to \\(12 \\times 2 = 24\\).\n\n5. **Day 4:**\n   - The number of bacteria doubles from \\(24\\) to \\(24 \\times 2 = 48\\).\n\n6. **Day 5:**\n   - The number of bacteria doubles from \\(48\\) to \\(48 \\times 2 = 96\\).\n\n7. **Day 6:**\n   - The number of bacteria doubles from \\(96\\) to \\(96 \\times 2 = 192\\).\n\nWe see that at the end of day 5, the colony has 96 bacteria, which is less than 100. At the end of day 6, the colony has 192 bacteria, which is more than 100. Therefore, the first day which ends with the colony having more than 100 bacteria is day 6.\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
