      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let \\( n \\) represent the first day which ends with the colony having more than 100 bacteria. The number of bacteria at the end of day \\( n \\) can be expressed as \\( 3 \\times 2^n \\).\n\nWe need to find the smallest \\( n \\) such that \\( 3 \\times 2^n > 100 \\).\n\nFirst, we solve the equation \\( 3 \\times 2^n = 100 \\) to estimate the value of \\( n \\):\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 2^n = 100\n\\]\n\nDividing both sides by 3:\n\n\\[\n2^n = \\frac{100}{3} \\approx 33.33\n\\]\n\nNext, we estimate \\( n \\) by solving the equation \\( 2^n \\approx 33.33 \\):\n\n\\[\n2^5 = 32 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 2^6 = 64\n\\]\n\nSince \\( 2^5 = 32 \\) is less than 33.33 and \\( 2^6 = 64 \\) is greater than 33.33, we conclude that \\( n \\) must be 6.\n\nTo verify, we calculate \\( 3 \\times 2^6 \\):\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 2^6 = 3 \\times 64 = 192\n\\]\n\nSince 192 is greater than 100, the number of the first day which ends with the colony having more than 100 bacteria is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
